{
  "$comment": [
    "Confusable real cards that must sit in the candidate pool, otherwise collisions",
    "are never exercised and top-1 accuracy is flattered. If the only 'Kozilek' in the",
    "pool is 'Kozilek, Butcher of Truth', resolving 'Kozilek' correctly proves nothing.",
    "",
    "Keyed by the testset card each group threatens. Many are genuine gameplay traps:",
    "Kozilek has two real faces, Ulamog has two, Atraxa has two, Nicol Bolas has four.",
    "Picking the wrong one is a real error, not a cosmetic one.",
    "",
    "generalPool is filler that shares no strong phonetic neighbourhood with the test",
    "set. It exists so the pool is not made up exclusively of near-misses, which would",
    "make the scoring pathologically hard and unrepresentative of a real decklist."
  ],
